{"name":"Pigskin Puffball","hex":"#e8dad1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pigskin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The skin of a pig.","Leather made from the skin of a pig."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pigskin"},{"term":"puffball","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various fungi, usually globose, that produce a cloud of brown dust-like spores from their mature fruiting bodies, especially in family Lycoperdaceae.","Any of various mushrooms with globose fruiting bodies."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puffball"}],"entries":[{"title":"Puffball","blocks":[{"text":"Puffballs are a type of fungus featuring a ball-shaped fruiting body that, when mature, bursts on contact or impact, releasing a cloud of dust-like spores into the surrounding area. Puffballs belong to the division Basidiomycota and encompass several genera, including Calvatia, Calbovista and Lycoperdon. The puffballs were previously treated as a taxonomic group called the Gasteromycetes or Gasteromycetidae, but they are now known to be a polyphyletic assemblage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Flaschenst%C3%A4ubling.jpg/330px-Flaschenst%C3%A4ubling.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puffball","wikidata":"Q1759052"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Calbovista_subsculpta_45731.jpg/500px-Calbovista_subsculpta_45731.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Calbovista_subsculpta_45731.jpg/1280px-Calbovista_subsculpta_45731.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Calbovista_subsculpta_45731.jpg/500px-Calbovista_subsculpta_45731.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaig